# Production build context — allowlist.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#
# docker/prod.Dockerfile copies the build context twice (`COPY . $APP_HOME` in
# the assets stage and again in the runtime stage). With a denylist, whatever
# untracked files the builder happened to have went into the image: on the
# machine ES-07 was built from, 180 MB of local scratch, and a developer's
# generated `jwks.b64.txt` with it (unresolved-items.md P2).
#
# ADR-0008 section 36 requires the production build context to be explicitly
# constrained and the artifact to be derived from known repository content. An
# allowlist is the only form that achieves it: a denylist can only exclude the
# categories someone thought of, and the failure mode of a missed category is a
# silently different image.
#
# BuildKit reads this file because it is named after the Dockerfile. The root
# .dockerignore applies to every other build in the repository.
#
# MAINTENANCE
#
# Adding a top-level file or directory that the running application needs means
# adding it here. `care.utils.tests.test_delivery_invariants` fails if an entry
# named here has disappeared from the repository, and
# `infrastructure/scripts/verify-image.sh` fails if the built image is missing
# the runtime assets, so a mistake in either direction surfaces in CI rather
# than in production.

# Exclude everything, then re-include what the application is made of.
*

# --- Python dependency manifests --------------------------------------------
!Pipfile
!Pipfile.lock

# --- Plugin installation (ADR: plug_config.py / install_plugins.py) ---------
!install_plugins.py
!plug_config.py
!plugs/

# --- Django project ---------------------------------------------------------
!manage.py
!care/
!config/

# --- Runtime role entrypoints (ES-06) ---------------------------------------
!scripts/

# --- Translation sources; catalogues are compiled in the assets stage -------
!locale/

# --- Reference data read by management commands -----------------------------
!data/

# --- Re-exclusions inside the allowed trees ---------------------------------
# Included by the directory rules above, but never part of an image.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
locale/**/*.mo
care/media/**
!care/media/.gitkeep
